course: dictionary
lesson: 11689
title: Attained: reached with effort
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Attained means reached or achieved. You usually attain something after hard work. «After months of practice, Maya attained her goal of swimming ten lengths.» The words months of practice are the clue: Maya worked hard, so attained means she reached her goal. Check it by swapping in reached: «Maya reached her goal» still makes sense.
explain: Attained can also mean reached a level, an age or a height. «The ball attained a height of 5 m.» The ball did not work hard to get there. It just went up as high as 5 m. Here attained means reached. Everyday speech usually says got or reached instead.
explain: You will often meet attained in school reports. «The student attained the expected standard in reading.» This means the student reached the level that was expected for their age. When you see attained, ask: what was reached, and was it a goal, a level, an age or a height?
fact: «Attained» means reached or achieved, usually after hard work.
fact: «Attain» is the basic form. «Attains» and «attaining» are the other forms of the same word.
fact: «Attained» can mean reached a level, age or height, as in «attained the age of ten».
fact: In everyday speech people often say «got» or «reached» instead of «attained».
fact: A good check is to swap in «reached» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Ravi attained the age of ten last month.» What does attained mean here? | Dropped | Forgot | Lost | *Reached
exercise: «After years of training, the team attained their goal.» What does attained suggest? | Given away for free | *Achieved after hard work | Broken into pieces | Lost during a game
exercise: «The rocket attained a height of 500 metres.» Find and copy one word that means reached. | metres | height | rocket | *attained
test: «The ball attained a height of 5 m.» What does this mean? | It fell below 5 m | It was painted 5 m long | *It reached a height of 5 m | It stayed still on the ground
test: Which word could replace attained in «She attained the expected standard»? | Lost | Forgot | Hid | *Achieved
exam: Which sentence uses attained correctly? | The puddle attained a loud noise | *The pupil attained the expected level in maths | Ben attained his lunch quickly | The cat attained a sleepy yawn
